    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1286">

                <pb facs="1240" n="1074" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1074"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/314</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-28T11:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 28, 1917—11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My June 27, 5 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1286-f1"/> Chihuahua Mining Company
                    received telegram last night from Chihuahua agent: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>We had to loan forcibly to the Government five thousand pesos which they
                            will discount from taxes. We could not avoid it.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Hard to justify this as they have ample money in Juarez and plan to run train
                    with military escort to Chihuahua to-day.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
